// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_dump64_defender_av_bypass_rename.yml
// ID Sigma: 129966c9-de17-4334-a123-8b58172e664d
// Título: Potential Windows Defender AV Bypass Via Dump64.EXE Rename
// Descripción: Detects when a user is potentially trying to bypass the Windows Defender AV by renaming a tool to dump64.exe and placing it in the Visual Studio folder.
Currently the rule is covering only usage of procdump but other utilities can be added in order to increase coverage.

// Fecha de creación: 2021-11-26
// Fecha de modificación: 2024-06-21
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: high
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_dump64_defender_av_bypass_rename.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath startswith ":\\Program Files" and FolderPath contains "\\Microsoft Visual Studio\\" and FolderPath endswith "\\dump64.exe") and (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "procdump" or (ProcessCommandLine contains " -ma " or ProcessCommandLine contains " -mp "))
